Falsifies `entropy_contract::verification::copying_writes_exactly_the_delivered_bytes`.

The defect: `copy_delivered_bytes` reads the reply word big-endian, the slip a reader makes who
takes the delivered bytes for the high end of the register. The count stays right and the bytes
come from the wrong end, so a short reply copies bytes the service never filled.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!` on `buffer[index]`, for a copy of one byte or more
whose word reads differently from each end.

diff --git a/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -264,7 +264,7 @@ pub const fn delivered_bytes(first_reply_word: u64) -> Option<usize> {
 /// value out and this copies bytes.
 pub fn copy_delivered_bytes(byte_count: usize, reply_word: u64, out: &mut [u8]) -> usize {
     let copied = byte_count.min(MAXIMUM_BYTES as usize).min(out.len());
-    out[..copied].copy_from_slice(&reply_word.to_le_bytes()[..copied]);
+    out[..copied].copy_from_slice(&reply_word.to_be_bytes()[..copied]);
     copied
 }
 
